{"title":"1962 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is given that one root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28d4a1a2e4d47884747ae2529e83200c86df24bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2 + rx + s = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> real numbers, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be4020c30477802a423676c651f9b0528387524e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/c/dac5dec897250384833e3c1b44639bf91cca823a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = \\sqrt{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" />). The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb3358659c476beac60abd09e3d0060533dad04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{undetermined} \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ 5 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\ -13 \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)}\\ 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"482\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If a quadratic with real coefficients has two non-real roots, the two roots must be complex conjugates of one another.\nThis means the other root of the given quadratic is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/923ad32cdda9ad8bc1ac7aa3741975ad15844c53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{3+2i}=3-2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />. \nNow Vieta's formulas say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6ca5fbfcfc64182918748f6eca8266ec2326fa5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to the product of the two roots, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c581a8c5e69e1325bef5e91282c4bc040b6455c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 2(3+2i)(3-2i) = \\boxed{26 \\textbf{ (E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"251\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME\" title=\"1962 AHSME\">1962 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1962 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?tit